        "uuid": "40e26f29_782af2e8",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-03T22:24:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "enum plz. Also, there\u0027s just no reason to use uint8_t. It\u0027s only likely to end in tears because Java makes it very difficult with a lack of unsigned support. It\u0027s almost certainly going to be aligned anyway, so it won\u0027t even save space over the binder.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 118,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 118,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "66c067313b5eebba5d8abc48504b4c4f1b9687a9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b63b5776_ca61276c",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1141163
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-06T22:32:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Its bit complicated to express it in enum because this byte contains 3 different parts. first part is precedence number (3 bits), 2nd part is (4 bits) is TOS and 3rd part (0) is unused as of now. Other option is to get all three parts separately and merge it in implementation which i think is unnecessary as its well defined in protocol.\n\nbtw, i can change it to int32_t",
      "parentUuid": "40e26f29_782af2e8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 118,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 118,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "66c067313b5eebba5d8abc48504b4c4f1b9687a9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ed4a18f_4be0bec3",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-06T22:36:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There may be a bitfield type for this? I can\u0027t remember. Suggest to check with smoreland@.",
      "parentUuid": "b63b5776_ca61276c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 118,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 118,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "66c067313b5eebba5d8abc48504b4c4f1b9687a9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "753b198a_c210dead",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1141163
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-07T17:35:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "you could pass the raw type e.g. int32_t around and document the structure. If subitems are each 16-bits, you could use two separate int16_t types, for instance\n\nSince the items are within a byte i would document it clearly",
      "parentUuid": "6ed4a18f_4be0bec3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 118,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 118,
        "endChar": 16
      },
